These are archives generated by LArc, the predecessor to LHA, which uses the
-lz5- compression algorithm.  Found in larc333.exe (self extracting archive):

    http://ftp.riken.go.jp/pub/pc/simtelnet/msdos/arcers/larc333.exe

lz4.lzs             - Archive containing uncompressed (stored) file.
lz5.lzs             - Archive containing -lz5- compressed file.
sfx.com             - Self extracting LArc archive.
long.lzs            - Archive containing a large compressed file.
subdir.lzs          - Archive containing subdirectories.
initial.lzs         - Crafted -lz5- archive that dumps the full initial
                      contents of the history buffer from the start of
                      decompression. This archive is confirmed to work
                      correctly with LArc v3.33. However, there are some
                      subtle differences in how later versions of LHarc
                      and LHA handle the -lz5- algorithm, and as a result
                      they do not extract it properly (see #66).

The following archives use the LArc 7 member header format, which stores a
two byte "level field" after the file name instead of the CRC-16 field.
They were generated by test/make_larc7_test_archives.py.

lz8.lzs             - Archive containing -lz8- compressed file.  This
                      method uses the same algorithm as -lz5-.
lz1.lzs             - Archive containing -lz1- compressed file.  This is
                      the bit oriented LZSS algorithm with a 2 KiB window
                      (11 bit position, 4 bit length).
lz2.lzs             - Archive containing -lz2- compressed file, using a
                      4 KiB window (12 bit position, 4 bit length).
lz3.lzs             - Archive containing -lz3- compressed file, using a
                      2 KiB window (11 bit position, 5 bit length).

